{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeRCKo5Svm2eTT3i5sdjw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Root cause\n\nThe failure isn't in `routes/public.map` itself — the map file correctly lists a specific `/health` entry ahead of the `/*` wildcard entry, and it's not being parsed at all in this code path.\n\nThe actual bug is in **`router/routes.go`**:\n\n```go\nfunc HealthHandler() string { return \"wildcard\" }\n```\n\n`HealthHandler()` is hardcoded to return `\"wildcard\"` instead of `\"health\"`. This is a source-level regression — the handler simply returns the wrong constant, unconditionally, regardless of routing logic. The test `TestHealthRoute` in `router/routes_test.go` expects `HealthHandler()` to return `\"health\"`, but gets `\"wildcard\"`, producing the failure message `\"shadowed by wildcard\"`.\n\nSo the fix belongs in `router/routes.go` (changing the return value to `\"health\"`), not in `routes/public.map`, which is already correctly configured."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":498,"cache_read_input_tokens":3395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":498},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2758d76c-eef7-4c11-a573-a66f20678323","uuid":"b4e3f50b-b467-48da-807a-88f89aa1cbb3","timestamp":"2026-08-26T10:23:44.777Z","request_id":"req_011CeRCKnP2o4SjFUgZ5G2bA"}
